  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia-Papua New Guinea Subnational Program (APSP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australia-Papua New Guinea (PNG) Subnational Program (APSP) utilises a placed-based approach to enhance the Australian Government&apos;s partnership with the Government of PNG at both national and subnational levels. The APSP focuses on strengthening subnational governance, human and economic development, gender equality, and disability inclusion. It coordinates Australia&apos;s whole of government efforts and program delivery in agreed locations across PNG. 
The APSP is an enabling facility and implementing mechanism for three placed-based program components: 1) Bougainville Partnership, INN958; 2) Kokoda Initiative Partnership, INN959; and 3) Western Province Partnership, INN929. The APSP also supports national decentralisation efforts and subnational governance activities in East Sepik, West Sepik, Morobe and Western Highlands.</narrative>
  </description>
